<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#one-party-state">Glossary</a> · Term · government</p><h1 class="enc-title">One-party state</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1918 CE – present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The one-party state, in which a single party monopolises power, emerged in Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after 1917 and became the form of communist, fascist and many post-colonial regimes. Its defenders claimed unity, stability and development; its record includes famines, terror and stagnation as well as rapid industrialisation.</p></div>
